---
/**
 * Demo-kit pattern shakedown page (hidden from production nav).
 *
 * Lives at /dev/demo-kit/ — only reachable by typing the URL. Used as
 * a build-time verification that the demo-kit primitives compile and
 * render correctly.
 */
import Layout from "../../layouts/Layout.astro";
import CodeReveal from "../../components/demo-kit/CodeReveal.astro";
import FavoritePage from "../../components/demo-kit/FavoritePage.astro";
import DemoChrome from "../../components/demo-kit/DemoChrome.astro";
import { PresetCarouselShakedown } from "../../components/demo-kit/PresetCarouselShakedown";
import { DemoKitShakedown } from "../../components/demo-kit/DemoKitShakedown";
import { GradientDescentVisualizer } from "../../components/demos/machine-learning/gradient-descent/GradientDescentVisualizer";
import algorithmSource from "../../components/demo-kit/__sample__/algorithm.ts?raw";
import gdAlgorithmSource from "../../components/demos/machine-learning/gradient-descent/algorithm.ts?raw";
import samplePage from "../../assets/sample-favorite-page.png";
---

<Layout
  title="Demo-kit shakedown — Engineering Portfolio"
  description="Internal page that exercises the demo-kit pattern."
>
  <article class="dev-page">
    <h1>Demo-kit shakedown</h1>
    <p>
      This page is a build-time check that the demo-kit primitives compile,
      render, and produce the expected HTML output.
    </p>

    <h2><code>&lt;CodeReveal&gt;</code> + <code>algorithm.ts?raw</code></h2>
    <p>
      The same <code>algorithm.ts</code> file is imported twice — once as a
      module (executable), once as raw text (displayable) — so what runs is
      exactly what's shown.
    </p>

    <CodeReveal code={algorithmSource} lang="typescript" />

    <h2><code>&lt;FavoritePage&gt;</code> handwritten thumbnail</h2>
    <p>
      A small, lazy-loaded thumbnail (AVIF + WebP + PNG via{" "}
      <code>astro:assets</code>) that opens a native <code>&lt;dialog&gt;</code>
      lightbox on click. Dismisses on Esc, click-outside, or mobile swipe-down.
    </p>

    <FavoritePage
      src={samplePage}
      caption="My first attempt at Problem 3a — Gradient Descent on a parabola, learning the update rule by hand."
    />

    <h2><code>&lt;DemoChrome&gt;</code> with share + GitHub link + about</h2>
    <p>
      Pine-tinted bordered card with title, "Try it" badge, share button (when
      <code>shareable</code>), always-present "View on GitHub" link, collapsed
      "About this demo" details, and a <code>&lt;noscript&gt;</code> fallback.
    </p>

    <DemoChrome
      title="Sample shakedown demo"
      shareable={true}
      demoSourcePath="site/src/pages/dev/demo-kit.astro"
      narration="A placeholder demo that does nothing visual, used to verify the demo-kit chrome renders correctly with all of its optional pieces enabled."
    >
      <div
        style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:120px;background:var(--color-math-bg);border-radius:8px;font-style:italic;color:var(--color-text-muted);"
      >
        (your interactive demo would render here)
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="about">
        This is a placeholder description that would normally explain the
        pedagogical purpose of the demo, list the controls, and note the
        relevant equations.
      </Fragment>
    </DemoChrome>

    <h3>Chrome with sharing disabled</h3>
    <DemoChrome
      title="Non-shareable variant"
      shareable={false}
      demoSourcePath="site/src/pages/dev/demo-kit.astro"
    >
      <div
        style="display:flex;align-items:center;justify-content:center;min-height:80px;background:var(--color-math-bg);border-radius:8px;font-style:italic;color:var(--color-text-muted);"
      >
        (no share button should appear in the footer)
      </div>
      <Fragment slot="about">
        Some demos opt out of URL-fragment sharing because their state isn't
        meaningfully shareable (e.g., a pure animation with no parameters).
      </Fragment>
    </DemoChrome>

    <h2><code>&lt;PresetCarousel&gt;</code> React island</h2>
    <p>
      Chip-based preset selector with ◀ Prev / Next ▶ controls. Doubles as
      desktop preset selector and touch-device fallback for canvas-drag demos.
      Hydrates on first visible.
    </p>

    <DemoChrome
      title="PresetCarousel shakedown"
      shareable={false}
      demoSourcePath="site/src/components/demo-kit/PresetCarousel.tsx"
      narration="Three named presets — Slow, Medium, Fast — selectable via chip clicks or the Prev/Next buttons. The current selection is reflected below the carousel."
    >
      <PresetCarouselShakedown client:visible />
      <Fragment slot="about">
        Demonstrates the demo-kit's preset-carousel primitive: keyboard-
        accessible chips with ≥44×44 px tap targets, wrap-around Prev/Next, and
        a React 19 island hydrated on visibility.
      </Fragment>
    </DemoChrome>

    <h2>
      <code>&lt;DemoCanvas&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;SliderRow&gt;</code> +
      <code>&lt;MathHud&gt;</code> + <code>&lt;DemoNarration&gt;</code>
    </h2>
    <p>
      All four #15 primitives wired together: a live oscillator with two slider
      controls, KaTeX HUD overlay, aria-live narration, and a draw-loop driven
      canvas with explicit width/height (zero CLS).
    </p>

    <DemoChrome
      title="Oscillator shakedown"
      shareable={false}
      demoSourcePath="site/src/components/demo-kit/DemoKitShakedown.tsx"
      narration="A sine wave whose frequency and amplitude are controlled by sliders. The HUD overlays the current parameters as KaTeX, and the narration line announces the state for screen-reader users."
    >
      <DemoKitShakedown client:visible />
      <Fragment slot="about">
        Validates the four core demo-kit primitives in concert:
        <code>&lt;DemoCanvas&gt;</code> (sized canvas + RAF draw loop),
        <code>&lt;SliderRow&gt;</code> (labeled native range with format +
        ticks), <code>&lt;MathHud&gt;</code> (KaTeX overlay), and
        <code>&lt;DemoNarration&gt;</code> (aria-live transcript).
      </Fragment>
    </DemoChrome>

    <h2>
      <code>&lt;GradientDescentVisualizer&gt;</code> — first real ML demo (#24)
    </h2>
    <p>
      The first hero ML demo, wired together from every demo-kit primitive:
      preset carousel, sized canvas with contour-shaded loss surface and
      animated trajectory, four sliders, KaTeX HUD, and aria-live narration.
      State serializes to the URL fragment via <code>useDemoState</code>.
    </p>

    <DemoChrome
      title="Gradient Descent Visualizer"
      shareable={true}
      demoSourcePath="site/src/components/demos/machine-learning/gradient-descent/GradientDescentVisualizer.tsx"
      narration="Interactive gradient descent on four named loss surfaces (Quadratic, Saddle, Rosenbrock, Plateau). Pick a preset or drag the sliders to explore how learning rate and momentum affect convergence."
    >
      <GradientDescentVisualizer client:visible />
      <Fragment slot="about">
        Shows momentum-augmented gradient descent on four canonical
        loss surfaces. Drag the sliders or pick a preset to see how
        learning rate (η) and momentum (β) interact, then watch the
        trajectory descend toward the minimum.
      </Fragment>
    </DemoChrome>

    <h3>Algorithm source (toggle to view)</h3>
    <p>
      The pure algorithm — <code>gradientDescentStep</code>,
      <code>isConverged</code>, <code>runDescent</code> — is exported from a
      separate module so the visualizer imports the same code that's displayed
      below.
    </p>
    <CodeReveal code={gdAlgorithmSource} lang="typescript" />
  </article>
</Layout>

<style>
  .dev-page {
    max-width: 70ch;
    margin: 2rem auto 4rem;
    padding: 0 1rem;
  }
  .dev-page h1,
  .dev-page h2,
  .dev-page h3 {
    font-family: "Source Serif 4 Variable", Georgia, serif;
  }
  .dev-page h2 {
    margin-top: 3rem;
  }
  .dev-page code {
    font-family: "JetBrains Mono Variable", monospace;
    background: var(--color-code-bg);
    padding: 0.125rem 0.375rem;
    border-radius: 4px;
    font-size: 0.875rem;
  }
</style>
